        <div class="trust-copy">
          <section><h2>The identity</h2><p class="about-creed">The art of probability. The science of edge. The power of compounding.</p><p>That is the whole philosophy in three sentences. <strong>Probability</strong>, because no single trade means anything on its own — only the distribution of many trades, taken together, decides an account. <strong>Edge</strong>, because an advantage is not an opinion; it is what remains of a strategy after every fee, charge, tax and funding payment has been subtracted, and it can be measured to the paise. <strong>Compounding</strong>, because small verified net edges, repeated with discipline and protected from leaks, are how accounts actually grow. Every tool Monks Of Market builds exists to serve those three sentences.</p></section>
          <section><h2>Why it exists</h2><p>Monks Of Market was built around a simple gap: many trading decisions begin with a target and end with a gross profit figure, while costs are considered too late. These calculators bring brokerage, exchange fees, GST, funding estimates, stop distance and other selected charges into the decision before entry.</p><p>The aim is not to predict markets or tell anyone what to trade. It is to make the arithmetic behind a trade easier to inspect.</p></section>
          <section><h2>Who writes this</h2><p>Monks Of Market is written by <strong>Kaizen</strong> — a retail trader who learned, the expensive way, that most trading education talks about entries while the real leak is in costs, probabilities and position sizing. Every guide here is written from that experience: claims are checked against verifiable numbers, and anything that cannot be verified is said plainly.</p><p>Kaizen is not SEBI-registered, not an investment adviser, research analyst, portfolio manager or tax professional — and nothing on this site is personal financial advice. The tools estimate; your broker, your exchange and your tax position decide.</p></section>
          <section><h2>What the tools cover</h2><h3>Crypto futures</h3><p>The crypto futures calculator estimates a USDT-settled position notional from a chosen risk budget and stop distance, then applies locked entry and exit fee rates, GST, estimated funding and an optional TDS cash-withholding estimate.</p><h3>Indian equity options</h3><p>The options calculator separates gross P&amp;L from brokerage, STT, exchange charges, SEBI turnover fees, stamp duty and GST. It also shows both a simple fee-recovery level and a dynamically solved breakeven.</p></section>
          <section><h2>How to use the output</h2><ul><li>Treat every result as an estimate, not an execution quote.</li><li>Review the visible assumptions; locked schedules are maintained by the Monks Of Market team and re-verified periodically — confirm that the displayed rates apply to your exchange, product, jurisdiction and tax position.</li><li>Use the result alongside independent research, official schedules and your own risk limits.</li></ul><div class="trust-callout"><strong>Editorial principle</strong>Specific numbers should be visible, sourced and open to challenge. If a rate cannot be verified for your trade, do not treat the preset as authoritative.</div></section>
          <section><h2>Independence</h2><p>Monks Of Market is an educational calculator, not a broker, exchange, investment adviser, portfolio manager, research analyst or tax adviser. No calculator result is a recommendation, signal, promise of performance or instruction to enter a trade.</p></section>
